  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I feel this canny may be controversial, because it involves potentially wiping out a huge swath of old vrchat content.\nVRChat has supported content from Unity 5.6 and onward. As wonderful as that is, it has allowed content that has broken due to time or version compatibility to break.\nI think vrchat should lock out content uploaded about 3 unity version's ago. At the current time that would be unity 5.3, which doesn't appear anyway now. When Unity 2019 rolls around that would remove 5.6 content.\nI believe this would be a way to healthily flush the ecosystem of old abandoned content, forcing this content to be thrown out in favor of updated content, but not so quickly that users have to constantly update.",
